  "text": "Born in Aleppo, Syria, one of the world’s oldest inhabited cities, Zahed draws deeply from its archaeological and cultural heritage. His work explores identity, history, and memory, shaped by Syria’s rich material culture and recent upheavals. Zahed’s precise ceramic practice reflects his archaeological expertise, creating richly textured, tactile forms. He masterfully transformed London’s construction clay into elegant, refined artworks, blending ancient sensibility with contemporary craft. For further information on pricing and availability for Zahed’s work, please contact info@goldenearthstudio.co.uk Artworks Bull's Matter by Zahed Tajeddin Bowing Bull By Zahed Tajeddin Elevation By Zahed Tajeddin Stillness By Zahed Tajeddin Back to Artists Bespoke Commissions Golden Earth Studio offers a bespoke commission service that utilises the construction byproducts of our clients’ homes. To explore the possibilities of commissioning a unique piece of artwork to compliments your interior space, get in touch via our contact form or email. info@goldenearthstudio.co.uk First & Last Name Email Phone Message Send",
